               "ir_export_window_help_long":  "IR windowing shapes the impulse response after frequency correction.\n\nIt affects ringing behavior, sidelobes, and effective time spread, but does not change the target curve or frequency-domain correction itself.\n\nHann provides stronger ringing control, while Tukey preserves more low-frequency energy with softer edges.\n\n A-FDW affects what is corrected; IR windowing affects how the correction is realized in time.",
