               "mode_advanced_label":  "Advanced (expert)",
               "mode_auto_desc":  "Automatic mode. Runs an automatic preset search and then creates the technically best possible filter. Select the filter type, sample rate, number of taps and HPF if you prefer it. CamillaFIR will calculate the target curve that best matches your measurements unless you explicitly choose your own target curve. Finally, press START. The values used can be found in the **summary.txt** file! If you run a second pass with the same settings, the program may improve the result by about 5%, depending on the room, because the cache stores an optimal starting point for the algorithm. The theoretical search space is enormous, so Automatic mode samples only a tiny subset and refines around the best candidates. Because the amount of computation is still very large, the speed of Automatic mode depends strongly on the performance of your computer.",
